d_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/570689331","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/3251#issuecomment-570689331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/3251","id":570689331,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MDY4OTMzMQ==","user":{"login":"jaki","id":16715704,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE1NzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16715704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki","html_url":"https://github.com/jaki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-01-03T20:30:01Z","updated_at":"2020-01-06T18:11:45Z","body":"I think that I have discovered the root cause.  On some code paths, the `DocKey` does not have a cotable id when it should.  This causes other weird bugs like an unwanted conflict between two different tables.\r\n\r\n| Session A | Session B |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| `CREATE TABLE t (i int, PRIMARY KEY (i ASC))` | |\r\n| `CREATE TABLE t2 (i int, PRIMARY KEY (i ASC))` | |\r\n| `INSERT INTO t VALUES (1)` | |\r\n| `INSERT INTO t2 VALUES (1)` | |\r\n| `BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ` | |\r\n| | `BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ` |\r\n| `SELECT 123` | |\r\n| | `SELECT 123` |\r\n| `SELECT * FROM t FOR UPDATE` | |\r\n| | `SELECT * FROM t2 FOR UPDATE` |\r\n| `COMMIT` | |\r\n| | `COMMIT` |\r\n\r\nOne of the commits conflicts when there should be no conflicts because each transaction acts on different tables.  This seems to stem from `EnumerateIntents` getting called with the key `SubDocKey(DocKey([], []), [])` rather than a key like `SubDocKey(DocKey(CoTableId=06400000-0000-0080-0030-000005400000, [], []), [])` in some cases.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/570689331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jaki","id":16715704,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE1NzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16715704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki","html_url":"https://github.com/jaki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"i